This is a project to build a re-ranker for the 3 tier recommender system
composed from:
   - TwoTowerDNN training
      (git@github.com:nking/recommender_systems.git)
      (https://www.kaggle.com/code/nicholeasuniquename/recommender-systems-with-tfx-pipelines)
      to make encoders for the query and candidates.  the encoders are used
      to make embeddings used in the retrieval and in the ranker cross-encoder.
   - the retrieval
      (in git@github.com:nking/retrieval.git but also in
      git@github.com:nking/ranker.git) uses an Approximate Nearest Neighbor
      library to find canididates to a query.
   - the ranker (GATv2 based cross-encoder)
      (git@github.com:nking/ranker.git)
      (https://www.kaggle.com/code/nicholeasuniquename/ranker-cross-encoder-w-gatv2)
     takes an input query and candidates, enriches them and returns
     a smaller subset of ranked candidates

This tier of the recommendation system takes the query, candidates, and
embeddings produced from the ranker cross-encoder, enriches the queries and returns
a re-ranked subset of the candidates it received.
A re-ranker provides more interaction between the query and candidate data
so can learn personalization better, but the runtime complexity is large
and so the previous stages of a recommender system are used to get a good but
small set of candidates to chose from rather than the whole product catalog.

This project creates a reranker cross-encoder by performing supervised-fine-tuning
to continue training a pretrained LLM that has instruction training.

The pretrained LLM with instruction training is:
Qwen/Qwen2.5-0.5B-Instruct available from
https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen2.5-0.5B-Instruct

Qwen2.5-0.5B-Instruct is a decoder-only transformer.

The model card states these abilities:
- instruction following,
- generating long texts (over 8K tokens),
- understanding structured data (e.g, tables),
- generating structured outputs especially JSON.
- improved resilience to the diversity of system prompts,
- enhanced role-play implementation and condition-setting for chatbots.
- Long-context Support up to 128K tokens
- ability to generate up to 8K tokens.

The instruction tuned model has these features:
Type: Causal Language Models
Training Stage: Pretraining & Post-training
Architecture: transformers with RoPE, SwiGLU, RMSNorm, Attention QKV bias and tied word embeddings
Number of Parameters: 0.49B
Number of Paramaters (Non-Embedding): 0.36B
Number of Layers: 24
Number of Attention Heads (GQA): 14 for Q and 2 for KV
Context Length: Full 32,768 tokens and generation 8192 tokens

